  "sha256_prefix": "361546ecf130",
  "two_worker_gap": "The 0.016 s format and 0.007 s pwrite figures were sums of per-piece times on one worker, not a split of the campaign sample. On the previous writer the two workers finished each piece together, so the wall was about that sum, and every sample also allocated and first-touched a fresh format buffer. That is the time between 0.016+0.007 and the 0.0347 s sample. Keeping the buffers across calls, and formatting eight ranges per worker so a pwrite is in flight during the next format, brings the 2-worker memory sample to 0.0232 s.",
  "mpi_bound": "Each rank is pinned to one core. Formatting the rank's slice and copying it into the page cache both need that core, so the wall stays near the sum. Two waves pwrite the first half while the second half is formatted; the copy does not leave the core, and an exclusive scan per wave is not free. Eight-rank tmpfs pwrite of the same 23.6 MB is about 0.008 s. The 8-rank memory write is 0.0145 s, the format plus that copy. Efficiency 0.8 at 8 ranks would need about 0.008 s, which is the pwrite ceiling and leaves no time for the format.",
